  1. answer_dataset (rag.py:179-184). After the loop, result["search_results"] and result["k"]
     read the last question, not the whole file, so you get a KeyError. It also never writes
     anything to save_directory. You need to keep the parsed file in its own variable, then write
     a StudentSearchResultsAndAnswer with model_dump_json. It also still uses raw json.loads +
     dicts; StudentSearchResults.model_validate_json would give you typed objects, as
     search_dataset does now.
  2. index --method hybrid (rag.py:96). HybridRetriever has no build_index, so you get an
     AttributeError. That means the indexes for hybrid have to be built in two runs (bm25, then
     dense), and both runs must use the same max_chunk_size. Otherwise the chunk_ids don't match
     and the fusion never lines up. The docstring says "Create the BM25 and Chroma indexes from
     the same chunks", but the code doesn't do that.
  3. The defaults are inconsistent. search defaults to bm25, but search_dataset and answer default
     to hybrid, so they fail until Chroma is indexed. Your todo says bm25 should be the default.
  4. An empty Chroma collection gives a TypeError (n_results=0), which is what you have right now.
     The fix is the count() == 0 guard I offered earlier.

